{
  "id": "ep201",
  "duration": 51.499,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.234,
      "text": "The undisputed largest star in the universe suddenly shrank in half.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "New shot of UY Scuti, the former largest known star v2.png",
        "credit": "User:21.Andromedae",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_shot_of_UY_Scuti,_the_former_largest_known_star_v2.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 1.533,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 1.533,
          "end": 4.233,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.234,
      "end": 12.979,
      "text": "In 2012, astronomers measured the supergiant star UY Scuti at 1,708 times the radius of our Sun.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "A Starry Combination.jpg",
        "credit": "ESO/J. Colosimo",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_Starry_Combination.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.233,
          "end": 9.333,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 9.333,
          "end": 12.967,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 12.979,
      "end": 18.474,
      "text": "Placed at the center of our solar system, its surface would swallow the orbit of Jupiter.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Solar System graphic by NASA.png",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Solar_System_graphic_by_NASA.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 12.967,
          "end": 18.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 18.474,
      "end": 25.794,
      "text": "That massive size estimate depended entirely on an assumed distance of 9,500 light-years.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Scutum (sct).jpg",
        "credit": "IAU and Sky & Telescope",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Scutum_(sct).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 18.467,
          "end": 22.0,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 22.0,
          "end": 25.8,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 25.794,
      "end": 33.014,
      "text": "But parallax data from the Gaia space telescope showed the star is actually 5,900 light-years away.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Artist's impression of the Gaia-ESO Survey (mpa-eso).tiff",
        "credit": "ESA/ESO",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artist%27s_impression_of_the_Gaia-ESO_Survey_(mpa-eso).tiff"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 25.8,
          "end": 30.367,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 30.367,
          "end": 33.0,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 33.014,
      "end": 40.489,
      "text": "In 2023, scientists recalculated its radius down to roughly 909 solar radii.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Betelgeuse vs V437 Sct vs UY Sct.png",
        "credit": "Spacetehman",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Betelgeuse_vs_V437_Sct_vs_UY_Sct.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 33.0,
          "end": 37.767,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 37.767,
          "end": 40.5,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 40.489,
      "end": 46.159,
      "text": "While still a pulsating monster destined for a supernova, its cosmic crown was gone.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Artist\u2019s impression of the red supergiant star Antares.jpg",
        "credit": "ESO/M. Kornmesser",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artist%E2%80%99s_impression_of_the_red_supergiant_star_Antares.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 40.5,
          "end": 42.967,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 42.967,
          "end": 46.167,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 46.159,
      "end": 51.149,
      "text": "A simple distance measurement proved even the biggest legend can vanish overnight.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "New shot of UY Scuti, the former largest known star v2.png",
        "credit": "User:21.Andromedae",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_shot_of_UY_Scuti,_the_former_largest_known_star_v2.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 46.167,
          "end": 51.5,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
